  "instructions": [
    "In a large mixing bowl, combine the ground pork, fish sauce, soy sauce, rice vinegar, chili flakes, garlic, and 1 tablespoon of sugar. Mix well until just combined. Let the mixture sit at room temperature for 30 minutes.",
    "Add the yeast, warm water, salt, and black pepper to the bowl and mix well until a sticky dough forms.",
    "Knead the dough for 5-7 minutes until it becomes smooth and elastic. Place the dough in a greased bowl, cover it with plastic wrap, and let it rise in a warm place for 1-2 hours, or until it has doubled in size.",
    "Preheat a grill or grill pan to medium-high heat. Divide the dough into 4 equal pieces and shape each piece into a ball. Flatten each ball into a disk shape and place it on the grill. Cook for 2-3 minutes per side, or until the bread is golden brown and crispy.",
    "While the bread is cooking, prepare the pickled carrots and daikon by slicing them thinly and mixing them with 1/4 cup of fish sauce, 1/4 cup of sugar, and 1/4 cup of rice vinegar. Let the mixture sit at room temperature for at least 30 minutes.",
    "Once the bread is cooked, let it cool for a few minutes before slicing it in half lengthwise. Spread 1 tablespoon of mayonnaise on the bottom half of the bread, followed by 1/4 cup of pickled carrots and daikon, 1/4 cup of sliced pork, 1/4 cup of fresh cilantro, and 1/4 cup of fresh mint. Top with the top half of the bread.",
    "Serve immediately and enjoy!"
  ],
